    {
      "id": 21,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        -680,
        0
      ],
      "size": [
        640,
        1000
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 20,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Qwen Image 2.1: inpainting, references\n\nRepaints the masked area of an image with Qwen Image 2.1 the way Forge's \"Inpaint upload\" does. **Inpaint Crop** cuts\nthe masked area with some context out of the image and scales it to the generation size, so that even a small area\nis sampled at full resolution; **Inpaint Stitch** scales the result back and blends it into the original through\nthe blurred mask. **Differential Diffusion** makes the soft mask edge blend gradually.\n\nRequires [ComfyUI-Inpaint-CropAndStitch](https://github.com/lquesada/ComfyUI-Inpaint-CropAndStitch) (install it with\nthe ComfyUI Manager).\n\n## Image Bench\n\nThe Generate tab is in **Inpaint** mode while this workflow is loaded.\n\n| Marker / node | Generate tab |\n|---------------|--------------|\n| `ib:img` Load Image | Input cell; \"Send image\" from Photoshop |\n| `ib:mask` Load Image Mask | Mask cell; the Photoshop selection |\n| `ib:cp`, `ib:pp`, `ib:np`, `ib:lora` | model, prompts, LoRAs (as in `image_qwen_image_2_1_txt2img.json`) |\n| `ib:smp` KSampler | seed, steps, CFG scale, sampling method, schedule type, denoising |\n| Inpaint Crop | Resize to (`output_target_width/height`), Mask blur (`mask_blend_pixels`), Mask mode (`mask_invert`) |\n| Only masked padding (Grow Mask) | Only masked padding, pixels |\n| Whole picture (Solid Mask) | Inpaint area: value 0 = Only masked, 1 = Whole picture |\n| `ib:ref:0-3` Reference 1-4 (bypassed) | References panel |\n\nThe loaders refer to the files the Photoshop plugin writes (`image_bench_photoshop_*.png`); send an image and a\nmask, or set them in the Input / Mask cells of the Generate tab, before the first queue.\n\n- **Only masked**: the model sees only the crop (the mask's bounding box plus the padding, widened to the aspect\n  ratio of the size). Describe what the crop shows, the new content of the masked area and its surroundings.\n- **Whole picture**: the whole image is scaled to the size and sampled; describe the whole image.\n- Denoising 0.85-1.0 replaces the content, 0.4-0.7 keeps its colors and shapes.\n- Mask blur widens the mask by that many pixels and blurs it; the pixels outside the mask within that distance are\n  blended too. Keep the size within about 1 MP with sides multiples of 32.\n\n**References** (up to 4; the encoder takes up to 16, connect more loaders marked `ib:ref:4`, ...): add images\nin the References panel of the Generate tab, by \"Ps sends to: reference\" from Photoshop, or by dropping them\nthere. They go into the `images` inputs of **Text Encode Qwen Image 2.1**, which shows them to the Qwen3-VL encoder\nand splices their VAE latents into the sequence (resized to about `resolution`² pixels). An empty slot is bypassed,\nwhich leaves its encoder input unconnected.\n\n## Model Links\n\n**diffusion_models**: [qwen_image_2.1_int8_convrot.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Qwen-Image-2.1/resolve/main/diffusion_models/qwen_image_2.1_int8_convrot.safetensors)\n**text_encoders**: [qwen3vl_8b_int8_convrot.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Qwen-Image-2.1/resolve/main/text_encoders/qwen3vl_8b_int8_convrot.safetensors)\n**vae**: [qwen_image_2.1_vae_bf16.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Qwen-Image-2.1/resolve/main/vae/qwen_image_2.1_vae_bf16.safetensors)\n\nQwen Image 2.1 is released under the Qwen Research License (non-commercial).\n"
      ],
      "title": "Note: Qwen Image 2.1 inpainting (Image Bench)",
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
